"whats_new.body" = "JackMoebius integration. JackMoebius, the functional successor of JackRouter (abandoned since 2020), is a virtual audio driver to install separately (link below). It exposes to the JACK graph the macOS apps with no native JACK support, both input and output, so they can talk to your JACK applications.\n\nNew in 2.1 (JackMoebius 1.1 or newer is required):\n\u2022  Input and output are set separately for each app: \u201cJackMoebius default\u201d (nothing to set in the app) or \u201cDedicated\u201d (a \u201cJackMoebius for <App>\u201d card). A small panel explains the effect before applying.\n\u2022  Up to 64 channels per app and per direction, out of 254 input and 254 output channels shared by all apps, with gauges to follow how full they are.\n\u2022  The shared input shows up in the patchbay: every app that reads it has its box with the two shared ports, and a cable is drawn in all of them.\n\u2022  Your cables are kept when an app changes mode or channel count.\n\u2022  Clear alerts (capacity almost full, daemon refusals explained, transport down, Mac default devices no longer JackMoebius), and the \u201cmaster\u201d button is gone.\n\nStudios: those saved with 2.0 reload as best they can; re-save them to move to the new format.";
"whats_new.changelog" = "Full changelog";
"whats_new.jackmoebius" = "Learn more about JackMoebius \u2197";
"whats_new.title" = "What's New in JackMate";

